Suomi
Svenska
Notifications
This device lets you know when you have new Rynke, and what you still need.
On for this device.
Off for this device.
Your device blocks notifications for RynkePoints. You can allow them in your browser&#39;s or device&#39;s settings.
On an iPhone, notifications only work once RynkePoints is on your home screen. Then open it from there.
This browser can&#39;t show notifications.
That didn&#39;t work. Please try again.
Animations
Animations when switching sections in Confetti and Disco
App
Install as an app
As an app on your iPhone: in Safari, tap &quot;Share&quot; and then &quot;Add to Home Screen&quot;.
As an app with Firefox: tap the menu ⋮ and then &quot;Install&quot; or &quot;Add to Home screen&quot;.
As an app on your Mac: in Safari, choose &quot;File&quot; &gt; &quot;Add to Dock&quot;.
Strava connection
Connected to Strava
Private activities count too.
Change permissions on Strava
Your consent
Agreed on 06/10/2026 (version 3.1).
We don&#39;t read GPS tracks, maps, photos or health data.
We only read the key figures of your rides, runs and swims, such as distance, time and elevation, and turn them into Rynke and badges.
The team sees your Rynke and, in the ranking, your sessions, kilometres and elevation, without your name. The organisers see them with your first name, plus your kilometres and elevation per day. Administrators see your first name and connection state.
All the details
From each ride we only read its name, sport type, start time, distance, moving time, elapsed time including pauses, elevation gain, whether it was entered manually or ridden on an indoor trainer, and whether Strava has flagged it.
Private (&quot;Only You&quot;) rides only count if you allow viewing your private activities on Strava.
We use the data only for Rynke and team events. Only you see your individual rides and their names.
The organisers see your first name from Strava, your Rynke and where they come from, what you still need, whether you&#39;ve reached your training goal, your team events and corrections, and which team events you reported you&#39;re coming to or were at.
The organisers also see, with your first name, how many kilometres you rode outdoors and virtually and how many metres of elevation you climbed, as a total per day, across the whole season. This includes private rides that count. They don&#39;t see your individual rides, their names, times or routes.
In the team&#39;s ranking everyone sees your number of counting rides, your kilometres and elevation per season, month and week, without your name. The organisers see, with your first name, your sessions per season and per day and your typical ride: the length half of your rides are above and half below. What we read from Strava doesn&#39;t change.
Administrators run the app for the team. They see your first name, whether you&#39;re connected and since when, when your club membership was last checked and whether your import is still running, but no rides or Rynke. They can remove you from the team: your data is then deleted, and only your Strava ID stays on a block list, so you can&#39;t connect to this team again.
Everyone else on the team sees your Rynke, overall and per week, without your name. Your kilometres and elevation count towards the team sums of the team badges, without your name. On which days and at what hour you ride, run or swim counts towards the team surprises, without your name.
You can leave at any time: in Settings, or by removing RynkePoints on Strava. We then delete all data about you, including your Rynke. If you leave the club, we delete it within 24 hours. Only if an administrator removes you do we keep your Strava ID, so you can&#39;t connect again.
Deleted data stays in our hosting provider&#39;s backups for up to 7 days.
We only set necessary cookies: for signing in and your language choice.
Notifications are optional, per device, and show only you how many Rynke are new and what you still need. They pass through the push service of your device&#39;s or browser&#39;s maker (e.g. Google, Apple, Mozilla, Microsoft). For this we store only the address it gives your device, and delete it when you turn them off, sign out or leave.
Rules
Rules version 3, in effect since 09/10/2026.
Everything from 01/01/2026 to 30/06/2027 counts.
The rules as PDF (in German)
Tours
Show the tour again
Account
Sign out
Sign out everywhere
